---
/*
 * Terms of Service (English) — 한국어 이용약관(src/pages/terms.astro)의 영문판입니다.
 * ⚠️ 한국어판을 고치면 이 파일도 함께 고치세요.
 */
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';

const { company, legal } = site;
const name = company.legalNameEn;
---

<DocLayout title="Terms of Service" meta={`Effective ${legal.effectiveDateEn}`}>
  <p class="note">
    This is an English translation of our Korean Terms of Service, provided for convenience. If the two versions differ, the Korean
    version applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-1">1. Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    These terms set out the rights, obligations, and responsibilities between {name} (“we”, “us”) and you when you use the Dearbe app
    (the “Service”).
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-2">2. Definitions</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>“Service” means the AI companion chat service we provide through our mobile app.</li>
    <li>“User” means a member who has agreed to these terms and uses the Service.</li>
    <li>“AI character” means a virtual conversation partner whose replies are generated by artificial intelligence.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="article-3">3. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms within the limits of applicable law. We'll announce changes in the app and on our website at least 7 days
    before they take effect, or 30 days before for changes that work against you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-4">4. Sign-up and age requirement</h2>
  <p>You must be 14 or older to sign up. If we find that you gave a false age, we may restrict your use of the Service.</p>

  <h2 id="article-5">5. About AI replies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Replies from AI characters are generated by artificial intelligence and may be inaccurate or untrue.</li>
    <li>AI characters don't provide medical, legal, financial, or other professional advice.</li>
    <li>
      If you're in crisis, please reach out to professionals. In Korea, call 109 (suicide prevention) or 1577-0199 (mental health crisis
      line). Elsewhere, contact your local emergency number.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="article-6">6. What you agree not to do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use someone else's information or register false information</li>
    <li>Try to make the Service produce illegal content or content that violates others' rights</li>
    <li>Get around the Service's safety features or access our systems without permission</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="article-7">7. Reporting content and restrictions</h2>
  <p>
    You can report inappropriate conversations or content in the app. We review reports and take action where needed, and we may
    restrict the accounts of users who break these terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-8">8. Paid features</h2>
  <p>
    Paid features are sold through Apple's In-App Purchase. Subscriptions, cancellations, and refunds follow Apple's policies and
    procedures. You can cancel a subscription anytime on your iPhone under <strong>Settings &gt; [your name] &gt; Subscriptions</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-9">9. Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account anytime in the app under <strong>Settings &gt; Account &gt; Delete Account</strong>. When you do, your
    personal information, including your chat history, is deleted as described in our Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-10">10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    We aren't liable when we can't provide the Service because of events beyond our control, such as natural disasters, or for damage
    caused by your own actions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="article-11">11. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea. Disputes arising from the Service will be resolved in the competent
    court under the Korean Civil Procedure Act.
  </p>

  <h3>Effective date</h3>
  <p>These terms take effect on {legal.effectiveDateEn}.</p>
</DocLayout>
